#import "../tcc.typ": bloco-resumo
#bloco-resumo(
  [ABSTRACT],
  [This document presents a general test of Typst features applied to academic document composition. Its purpose is to observe the behavior of front matter, main text, back matter, formatting, and automation in a single compiled file. The method consists of using an existing experimental template with fictional data and demonstration content. The test includes hierarchical headings, long paragraphs, citations, a bibliography, a figure with caption and source, a table, a text box, a list, a footnote, and a mathematical expression. It also makes it possible to inspect the table of contents, pagination, page breaks, and modular inclusion of external files. The results must be visually checked after compilation in the Windows environment used by the project. This document does not establish full compliance with SENAI-SP or ABNT standards; it is intended to identify working features, compilation problems, and presentation differences that require later correction.],
  [Keywords],
  "Typst; academic formatting; composition test; PDF generation",
)
